  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 104.13 Scrub-shrub wetland",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 104.13 “Scrub-shrub wetland” means a wetland dominated by woody vegetation less than 20 feet tall, such as true shrubs, young trees, and trees or shrubs that are small or stunted because of environmental conditions, as determined using the federal classification method.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes #1, #2, #3, and #4 at Chapter heading for Env-Wt 100) #12801, eff 12-15-19",
